1
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:11,830
Everyone.

2
00:00:11,830 --> 00:00:17,540
I know everyone here worked hard
for today's performance.

3
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:18,500
Kotono.

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,790
Yes.

5
00:00:19,790 --> 00:00:20,750
Sakura.

6
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:21,910
Yes.

7
00:00:21,910 --> 00:00:22,950
Rei.

8
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:23,950
Yes.

9
00:00:23,950 --> 00:00:25,040
Nagisa.

10
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:26,250
Yes.

11
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:27,370
Suzu.

12
00:00:27,370 --> 00:00:28,910
Yes, indeed.

13
00:00:28,910 --> 00:00:29,830
Saki.

14
00:00:29,830 --> 00:00:31,040
Yes.

15
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:31,950
Chisa.

16
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:33,540
Y-Yes.

17
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:34,790
Shizuku.

18
00:00:34,790 --> 00:00:35,950
Yeah.

19
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:37,040
Miss Haruko.

20
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:38,330
Yes.

21
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:39,370
Mei.

22
00:00:39,370 --> 00:00:41,290
Yup!

23
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:45,200
To be honest, technique-wise,
we're far from perfect.

24
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:50,160
But all your efforts up until today
are engraved in you.

25
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:54,410
Give it everything you've got
now for this performance!

26
00:00:54,410 --> 00:00:55,580
Yes!

27
00:01:00,870 --> 00:01:02,830
Ready Kotono?

28
00:01:02,830 --> 00:01:04,040
Yeah.

29
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:11,750
Hoshimi Productions!

30
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:12,700
--Let's...
--...go!

31
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:13,830
Fight!

32
00:01:13,830 --> 00:01:17,290
Go, go, go! Yeah!

33
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,160
This stage is our very first step.

34
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:31,330
Are you watching...

35
00:01:31,330 --> 00:01:32,750
...Mana?

36
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,000
"5 YEARS AGO"

37
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
"Hoshimi High School"

38
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,500
"Congratulations           "Welcome         "Spring
on your admission!"    New Students!"    Festival"

39
00:01:46,330 --> 00:01:48,450
Hey, new students!

40
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:53,700
Promise me you'll make the next three years
an unforgettable high school experience!

41
00:01:57,790 --> 00:01:58,540
--The light and shadow of youth.

42
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:01,160
--Next, each club will be coming up
to promote themselves!
--The light and shadow of youth.

43
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,700
--Next, each club will be coming up
to promote themselves!
--Of course, she's the light and I'm...

44
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:04,830
--Make sure to stay for it
if you're still undecided.
--Of course, she's the light and I'm...

45
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:05,410
--Makino, hurry up!

46
00:02:05,410 --> 00:02:07,410
--But I'd recommend staying for it
even if you've decided, too!
--Makino, hurry up!

47
00:02:07,410 --> 00:02:08,160
--But I'd recommend staying for it
even if you've decided, too!
--Coming!

48
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:11,700
They go all out for these presentations,
so please check them out!

49
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:15,160
After that, we'll move on to
the fun recreational activities!

50
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:23,370
Light and shadow don't mix inherently...

51
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:31,580
Why is she sitting next to me?

52
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:32,700
It's science next.

53
00:02:32,700 --> 00:02:35,080
I'm so going to fall asleep!

54
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:36,410
After class?

55
00:02:36,410 --> 00:02:37,500
Yup.

56
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:40,330
I want to talk to you about something.

57
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,330
It can't be now?

58
00:02:48,330 --> 00:02:50,080
No!

59
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:51,870
Listen.

60
00:02:51,870 --> 00:02:55,370
I better see you after school!

61
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:01,200
What was that about?

62
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:05,040
The emperor has abdicated

63
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:06,620
and by next autumn,

64
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:08,620
--As far as these things go...
--he shaved his head
and entered priesthood.

65
00:03:08,620 --> 00:03:12,700
--It's usually a confession...
--He wandered the mountains
here and there

66
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:15,660
--No... There's no way that would happen to me.
--and devoted himself
to Buddhist training.

67
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:16,200
--The narrator speaks in a distinct tone
regarding the emperor.

68
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:18,750
--It must be one of those pranks or something.
--The narrator speaks in a distinct tone
regarding the emperor.

69
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:19,250
--They have great respect
towards the emperor.

70
00:03:19,250 --> 00:03:21,910
--Do people still do those things?
--They have great respect
towards the emperor.

71
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,500
This will be on the test.

72
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:25,370
I guess so...

73
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:32,160
A prank?

74
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:33,370
What is?

75
00:03:33,370 --> 00:03:35,870
What do you mean? Um...

76
00:03:35,870 --> 00:03:36,950
This scenario...

77
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:39,370
I'm not sure what you're talking about.

78
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:45,620
Anyway, I have a favor to ask you, Makino.

79
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:50,660
An idol...?

80
00:03:50,660 --> 00:03:51,830
Yeah...

81
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:54,330
Is that weird?

82
00:03:54,330 --> 00:03:55,370
No.

83
00:03:55,370 --> 00:03:58,540
I was just surprised because it was abrupt.

84
00:03:58,540 --> 00:04:01,950
But well, I'd say you can become one.

85
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:04,910
Nagase, you can be an idol.

86
00:04:04,910 --> 00:04:06,950
I think it would suit you, Nagase.

87
00:04:06,950 --> 00:04:08,160
It's Mana!

88
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:09,540
What?

89
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:11,160
Just call me Mana.

90
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:13,160
Everyone else calls me that, too.

91
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:15,040
What... Um...

92
00:04:15,040 --> 00:04:16,410
That's a bit...

93
00:04:16,410 --> 00:04:19,120
It's totally fine!

94
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:25,120
All right...

95
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,540
Then...

96
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:27,790
Mana.

97
00:04:27,790 --> 00:04:29,040
Good!

98
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:31,080
Then, Makino...

99
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:36,000
Oh, my first name is Kohei.

100
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,540
I knew that.

101
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:39,290
You can call me Kohei, too.

102
00:04:39,290 --> 00:04:41,120
No, that would be weird.

103
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:43,580
I'm calling you Makino, okay?

104
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:45,790
If we call each other by our
first names out of the blue,

105
00:04:45,790 --> 00:04:47,790
everyone would get suspicious.

106
00:04:47,790 --> 00:04:49,660
That doesn't make any sense.

107
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:51,790
So...

108
00:04:51,790 --> 00:04:57,750
It seems like the person who
scouted me is a famous producer.

109
00:04:57,750 --> 00:04:59,040
Nagas--

110
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:02,830
That probably happens to you a lot, Mana.

111
00:05:02,830 --> 00:05:04,830
That's not true.

112
00:05:04,830 --> 00:05:09,370
It's never happened to me before,
so I don't know what to do.

113
00:05:09,370 --> 00:05:11,790
But I am interested...

114
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:15,910
So I thought about it a lot
and consulted my little sister...

115
00:05:15,910 --> 00:05:18,200
So, why me...?

116
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:20,290
W-Well.

117
00:05:20,290 --> 00:05:24,620
Boys can be knowledgeable about idols, right?

118
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:28,450
It's not like all the guys are...

119
00:05:28,450 --> 00:05:32,370
There's that complicated
Venus-something system, right?

120
00:05:32,370 --> 00:05:36,540
I thought I'd consult someone
knowledgeable about that.

121
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:38,750
I'm not knowledgeable at all, either.

122
00:05:38,750 --> 00:05:42,410
I would ask Furuta or Kawano about that--

123
00:05:42,410 --> 00:05:44,660
I'm asking you, Makino!

124
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:52,040
I haven't told anyone else about this,

125
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:53,620
so don't tell anyone, okay?

126
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:56,750
I don't get it... Why me?

127
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:58,790
That's because...

128
00:06:03,290 --> 00:06:06,660
You sit right next to me and it was convenient!

129
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:08,910
Purely proximity, huh?

130
00:06:13,450 --> 00:06:17,250
So... About that favor I wanted to ask...

131
00:06:17,250 --> 00:06:18,540
Yeah.

132
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:20,750
Actually...

133
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:27,660
"Hoshimi Productions"

134
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:31,750
Kohei Makino, a second-year in high school.

135
00:06:31,750 --> 00:06:33,750
So you're classmates with Mana?

136
00:06:33,750 --> 00:06:35,120
Yes.

137
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:36,950
What's your relationship?

138
00:06:36,950 --> 00:06:38,370
Well...

139
00:06:38,370 --> 00:06:40,660
We sit right next to each other.

140
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:42,290
Sit next to each other?

141
00:06:42,290 --> 00:06:43,620
That's it?

142
00:06:43,620 --> 00:06:44,950
Naga--

143
00:06:44,950 --> 00:06:48,620
Mana and I've never really spoken at school...

144
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:50,660
That's not true!

145
00:06:50,660 --> 00:06:52,540
We've spoken three times...

146
00:06:52,540 --> 00:06:55,450
Or was it twice...?

147
00:06:56,870 --> 00:06:59,750
Are you familiar with the Venus Program?

148
00:06:59,750 --> 00:07:02,330
Yes, the general idea of it.

149
00:07:02,330 --> 00:07:05,540
It's a ranking system for idols, right?

150
00:07:05,540 --> 00:07:06,500
That's right.

151
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:12,000
Based on various data like popularity,
performance, and audience reaction,

152
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:16,080
an AI makes a judgment and
spits out the numeric data.

153
00:07:16,080 --> 00:07:17,750
An AI...?

154
00:07:17,750 --> 00:07:21,660
It's an attempt to have idols
compete under equal conditions.

155
00:07:21,660 --> 00:07:24,200
It's sounding more like a sports game.

156
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:28,620
We'll be registering idols from our
agency in the Venus Program, too.

157
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:30,450
Mana, too, of course.

158
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:35,370
It's true that we're short-handed.

159
00:07:35,370 --> 00:07:38,620
We'll have to hire someone eventually
to keep things running.

160
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:42,080
Since you're in school, you'll be
part-time until you graduate.

161
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:44,580
What? So that means...

162
00:07:44,580 --> 00:07:46,250
You're hired.

163
00:07:46,250 --> 00:07:48,910
Thank you very much, President.

164
00:07:48,910 --> 00:07:52,330
That's too stuffy, just call me Saegusa.

165
00:07:52,330 --> 00:07:57,580
To hire you part-time was one of the conditions
to get Mana to sign with us, anyway.

166
00:07:57,580 --> 00:07:59,660
--Hey!
--What?

167
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:01,540
We had already decided to hire you.

168
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:05,120
Mr. Saegusa, you promised you wouldn't tell!

169
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:06,290
Oh, yeah?

170
00:08:06,290 --> 00:08:07,750
Gosh!

171
00:08:13,830 --> 00:08:15,750
Mana, I'm coming in.

172
00:08:15,750 --> 00:08:17,000
Okay!

173
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,040
It's almost time for rehears--

174
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:29,160
What do you think?

175
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:30,620
It's... all right.

176
00:08:30,620 --> 00:08:32,540
Look at me and say it.

177
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:33,950
I am looking.

178
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:36,750
How would you rate me out of 100?

179
00:08:36,750 --> 00:08:38,450
Eighty-five...

180
00:08:38,450 --> 00:08:42,910
Apparently, not being able to say 100
is the nature of Japanese people.

181
00:08:42,910 --> 00:08:47,290
If I rated you 100 already,
what happens when you improve?

182
00:08:47,290 --> 00:08:49,410
I, Mana Nagase,

183
00:08:49,410 --> 00:08:53,160
will aim to be an idol that can't
be rated on a 100-point-scale!

184
00:08:55,540 --> 00:08:58,500
Miss Nagase, it's time for rehearsal!

185
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,910
Coming!

186
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:53,750
"Newcomer Award"

187
00:10:04,330 --> 00:10:05,830
"Idol Championship"

188
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,830
Pretty soon, I'll be a high school graduate.

189
00:10:08,830 --> 00:10:10,790
Time flew by quick!

190
00:10:10,790 --> 00:10:11,910
Oh, yeah!

191
00:10:11,910 --> 00:10:13,790
Let's go for a drive soon!

192
00:10:13,790 --> 00:10:16,450
Hey! Don't talk to me right now.

193
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:17,790
I just got my driver's license...

194
00:10:17,790 --> 00:10:19,910
Here, say, "ah."

195
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:29,870
We're gonna be even busier after we graduate.

196
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:32,000
So you better brace yourself!

197
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:34,450
You better not forget you said that.

198
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:38,700
Graduate representative, Mana Nagase.

199
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:41,410
"Graduation"

200
00:10:38,700 --> 00:10:41,410
Graduate representative, Mana Nagase.

201
00:10:41,410 --> 00:10:42,700
Yes!

202
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:48,290
During my six years attending
Hoshimi Junior High and High School,

203
00:10:48,290 --> 00:10:51,040
I've had various encounters.

204
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:56,660
Each encounter contributed to who I am today
and led to my current entertainment career.

205
00:10:56,660 --> 00:11:00,950
I am grateful for the open-minded
teachers at this school...

206
00:11:00,950 --> 00:11:01,950
Senpai!

207
00:11:01,950 --> 00:11:03,910
Congratulations on graduating!

208
00:11:03,910 --> 00:11:05,750
Are you staying for the concert?

209
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:07,250
"Mana Nagase Special Concert Stage"

210
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:07,250
Of course!

211
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:09,750
"Mana Nagase Special Concert Stage"

212
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:09,750
It's a privilege as a
Hoshimi High School student.

213
00:11:09,750 --> 00:11:12,700
Happy graduation, Makino.

214
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:14,750
Congratulations, Mana.

215
00:11:17,750 --> 00:11:19,370
Well, I better go!

216
00:11:19,370 --> 00:11:24,290
Make sure you watch my last
concert as a high school student!

217
00:11:24,290 --> 00:11:25,540
I will.

218
00:11:38,410 --> 00:11:40,370
Wow!

219
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:48,040
After graduating high school,
I was promoted from a part-time

220
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:50,790
to a full-time employee at Hoshimi Productions.

221
00:11:50,870 --> 00:11:53,370
"Hoshimi Productions"

222
00:11:53,370 --> 00:11:54,250
"Reception Room"

223
00:11:54,250 --> 00:11:58,330
The 14th Next Venus Grand Prix.

224
00:11:58,330 --> 00:12:01,250
Will we be entering it this time?

225
00:12:01,250 --> 00:12:04,000
I'll leave that decision to both of you.

226
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,790
Why didn't we enter it last year?

227
00:12:06,790 --> 00:12:09,450
I deemed it was too early.

228
00:12:09,450 --> 00:12:13,200
The Venus Grand Prix is
limited to newcomer idols only.

229
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:17,660
"14TH NEXT VENUS GRAND PRIX
Project Proposal"

230
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:17,660
If I win, I instantly join
the ranks of top idols.

231
00:12:17,660 --> 00:12:20,790
Your current popularity doesn't apply.

232
00:12:20,790 --> 00:12:25,040
Every participant starts off
from an equal baseline.

233
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:27,620
It will test your true abilities.

234
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:29,200
Um, I think I'll--

235
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:31,410
--I'll enter!
--What?

236
00:12:31,410 --> 00:12:32,660
Let's do this!

237
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:34,910
You are my senior, Haruko!

238
00:12:34,910 --> 00:12:36,160
It's our chance!

239
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:38,540
Only by two months...

240
00:12:39,870 --> 00:12:41,830
Well, if you are entering...

241
00:12:41,830 --> 00:12:44,620
I'll make sure I win, of course!

242
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:47,660
Haruko and I will both participate!

243
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:49,660
What?! What?!

244
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:51,370
M-Mana...

245
00:12:51,370 --> 00:12:52,870
Let's do this together!

246
00:12:52,870 --> 00:12:55,080
--All right!
--Oh, no...

247
00:12:58,910 --> 00:13:01,120
I'm so nervous.

248
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:16,580
Do you have the confidence
to defeat all these rivals?

249
00:13:16,580 --> 00:13:18,790
Who do you think I am?

250
00:13:18,790 --> 00:13:20,580
Jeez.

251
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:23,160
You haven't changed at all, huh?

252
00:13:23,160 --> 00:13:24,790
I can't afford to lose at this point.

253
00:13:24,790 --> 00:13:27,750
I want to meet everyone's expectations.

254
00:13:27,750 --> 00:13:30,580
For Haruko, who unfortunately lost...

255
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:32,830
For Mr. Saegusa and the staff...

256
00:13:32,830 --> 00:13:37,160
And most importantly,
for my fans who support me.

257
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,120
You're right.

258
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:41,700
And plus a little for you, too, Makino.

259
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:43,450
I'm just an after-thought, huh?

260
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:49,950
This is as far as I go every time.

261
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:55,540
I can only watch you from here.

262
00:13:55,540 --> 00:13:58,120
That's your job right, Makino?

263
00:14:01,950 --> 00:14:03,620
Yeah.

264
00:14:03,620 --> 00:14:05,370
Plus...

265
00:14:05,370 --> 00:14:07,450
You being there...

266
00:14:07,450 --> 00:14:10,540
...could be a source of power for me.

267
00:14:10,540 --> 00:14:12,120
Here I go!

268
00:14:15,410 --> 00:14:18,500
"Mana Nagase"

269
00:14:20,580 --> 00:14:21,620
She did it!

270
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:23,580
Go, Mana!

271
00:14:44,700 --> 00:14:47,410
"Mana Nagase"

272
00:15:00,870 --> 00:15:05,500
"Hoshimi Productions"

273
00:15:06,750 --> 00:15:09,200
It's the monumental final round.

274
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:12,410
I wanted you to take me there, Makino.

275
00:15:12,410 --> 00:15:14,540
The traffic seems to be bad right now.

276
00:15:14,540 --> 00:15:17,200
You better be there for my performance!

277
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:19,540
I'll head over as soon as I finish this errand.

278
00:15:19,540 --> 00:15:21,620
All right, then.

279
00:15:21,620 --> 00:15:25,580
I won't forgive you for being late,
even if you apologize.

280
00:15:25,580 --> 00:15:26,500
Mana.

281
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:30,750
You made it to the final round.

282
00:15:30,750 --> 00:15:33,120
You really are amazing.

283
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:39,500
Doing what I said I would is my policy.

284
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:41,790
Have I ever said any lies?

285
00:15:41,790 --> 00:15:43,750
Lots of them.

286
00:15:43,750 --> 00:15:45,200
Did I really?

287
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:50,250
You better be there no matter what, Makino.

288
00:15:50,250 --> 00:15:52,750
If you're not there...

289
00:15:59,790 --> 00:16:02,080
I'll be waiting for you.

290
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:03,870
Sorry for the wait.

291
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:20,910
It's true that she said a bunch of little lies.

292
00:16:20,910 --> 00:16:25,290
But she never told a big lie.

293
00:16:25,290 --> 00:16:28,410
Mana declared that she'd win.

294
00:16:28,410 --> 00:16:32,000
Because she did, she really would.

295
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,080
That's how it felt.

296
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:34,750
Excuse me!

297
00:16:36,450 --> 00:16:39,410
Are you from Hoshimi Productions?

298
00:16:39,410 --> 00:16:41,290
Yes, I am.

299
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,160
Still nothing?

300
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:45,040
Come on.

301
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:46,290
They're taking too long.

302
00:16:46,290 --> 00:16:48,620
It could be part of the performance.

303
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:55,040
"Hoshimi General Hospital"

304
00:16:59,540 --> 00:17:02,290
"East Tower | West Tower"
"Emergency Room | Internal Medicine"
"Endoscopy Center | Cardiology"

305
00:17:05,790 --> 00:17:08,790
"OPERATION IN SESSION"

306
00:17:11,950 --> 00:17:18,330
Mana's accidental death became the biggest news
of the year when it reached the press.

307
00:17:18,330 --> 00:17:19,500
And so...

308
00:17:19,500 --> 00:17:25,120
The final round of the 14th
Next Venus Grand Prix

309
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:27,370
never commenced.

310
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:32,040
"2 YEARS AGO"

311
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:34,950
"Hoshimi Productions"

312
00:17:35,790 --> 00:17:38,580
Makino?

313
00:17:38,580 --> 00:17:40,370
Makino.

314
00:17:40,370 --> 00:17:41,620
Oh, yes?

315
00:17:41,620 --> 00:17:43,700
Is that your phone?

316
00:17:45,660 --> 00:17:48,040
Yes, thank you for your call.

317
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:50,120
Yes, yes.

318
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:29,200
Being in the industry can make you
develop weird habits.

319
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:36,410
The day of the accident, I thought in the back
of my mind I was being involved in a prank.

320
00:18:36,410 --> 00:18:40,580
The day of the final round...
She was sent off by herself...

321
00:18:40,580 --> 00:18:42,370
The conditions were perfect.

322
00:18:46,830 --> 00:18:49,290
Nothing's changed.

323
00:18:51,450 --> 00:18:54,000
The instigator is Mana herself.

324
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:58,870
She'll come out laughing at
my dumbfounded face.

325
00:18:58,870 --> 00:19:02,410
I would've been really mad.

326
00:19:02,410 --> 00:19:03,870
But...

327
00:19:03,870 --> 00:19:05,910
Even then...

328
00:19:05,910 --> 00:19:07,950
That would've been...

329
00:19:07,950 --> 00:19:09,620
...a lot more...

330
00:19:12,910 --> 00:19:14,200
Makino.

331
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:23,160
No way.

332
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:25,700
Makino, over here.

333
00:19:29,160 --> 00:19:31,080
Did I surprise you?

334
00:19:33,450 --> 00:19:36,200
Mana...

335
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:44,750
Hey... So, it was a prank.

336
00:19:46,330 --> 00:19:48,910
Suspicious as always, I see.

337
00:19:48,910 --> 00:19:53,000
We've known each other so long,
let's have a little more trust.

338
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:57,160
Then stop doing things to startle me.

339
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:58,830
You're right.

340
00:19:58,830 --> 00:19:59,950
Sorry!

341
00:20:00,580 --> 00:20:04,370
That day, I met Mana again.

342
00:20:04,370 --> 00:20:06,700
This time, as a ghost.

343
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:12,580
"TODAY"

344
00:20:14,700 --> 00:20:16,910
Morning!

345
00:20:16,910 --> 00:20:19,080
Well, don't you seem fired up?

346
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:20,910
Of course I am.

347
00:20:20,910 --> 00:20:22,620
Interview day, was it?

348
00:20:23,620 --> 00:20:25,330
What is it?

349
00:20:25,330 --> 00:20:30,120
You look more like an interviewee
than an interviewer.

350
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:31,620
Well, excuse me.

351
00:20:31,620 --> 00:20:34,500
But I'm three years older now,

352
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:36,040
unlike you.

353
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:38,330
Ghosts don't age!

354
00:20:38,330 --> 00:20:40,790
You can still grow mentally.

355
00:20:40,790 --> 00:20:43,120
I've been growing, thank you very much.

356
00:20:43,120 --> 00:20:46,080
I'm a ghost, so let me take my time.

357
00:20:46,080 --> 00:20:49,830
I feel like you're becoming more
and more of a slacker.

358
00:20:49,830 --> 00:20:53,410
You used to shine brightly back in the day.

359
00:20:53,410 --> 00:20:56,950
You know that's a taboo thing
to say to a popular idol!

360
00:20:56,950 --> 00:20:59,870
That was when you were alive, right?

361
00:21:04,660 --> 00:21:06,750
Were you doing interviews today?

362
00:21:06,750 --> 00:21:07,750
Yes.

363
00:21:07,750 --> 00:21:10,410
There may be a great increase in junior idols.

364
00:21:10,410 --> 00:21:12,500
I'm happy to hear that.

365
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:14,040
Thank you very much.

366
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:18,160
But it gets me thinking of
my future career, too.

367
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:21,330
I'm sorry that I've been so useless...

368
00:21:21,330 --> 00:21:22,830
That's not what I meant.

369
00:21:22,830 --> 00:21:26,080
That's right. It's all your fault, Makino.

370
00:21:26,080 --> 00:21:29,080
You're failing to bring out Haruko's charms.

371
00:21:29,080 --> 00:21:30,290
I agree...

372
00:21:30,290 --> 00:21:31,120
Huh?

373
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:33,950
I'm sorry, I was talking to myself!

374
00:21:33,950 --> 00:21:35,660
Dummy.

375
00:21:35,660 --> 00:21:38,790
I wonder what kind of girls we'll see today.

376
00:21:38,790 --> 00:21:40,830
I'm looking forward to it.

377
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:44,580
"Hoshimi Productions"

378
00:22:05,330 --> 00:22:06,750
Are you okay?

379
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:09,870
Thanks...

380
00:22:13,080 --> 00:22:17,080
"From This First Step"

